# Real subscriber files hold ntfy topics, which are open pub/sub: anyone
# who learns the name can publish to that person's phone. They belong in
# the private runner repo, never in this public one.
#
# The whole directory is ignored, and the template lives outside it as
# users.example.toml, so that `dispatch --users ./users` can never pick
# up a placeholder file and push to a public topic.
users/
